[{:doc/type :manual-rollback-decision-tree
  :doc/id "month-3-manual-rollback-decision-tree"
  :doc/title "Month 3 Manual Rollback Decision Tree — Owner Discretion & SLA (2026-09-11 to 2026-09-14)"
  :doc/date "2026-07-21"
  :doc/author "Claude Code Agent"
  :doc/status "ACTIVE"

  :decision-tree/overview
  "This document guides the canary-lead (owner) through manual rollback decisions.
   Automatic triggers handle most failures autonomously; manual decisions are for edge cases
   where the owner judges that proceeding (despite SLO risk) offers greater business value
   than immediate rollback. Manual override has a strict 15-minute SLA (max delay before
   rollback executes)."

  :decision-tree/when-manual-decision-needed
  {:automatic-triggers-fire
   "If any automatic trigger fires (latency, parity, reliability, memory),
    the rollback executes automatically without waiting for owner decision."
   :manual-decision-scenarios
   ["Owner sees SLO violation trending but not yet at automatic trigger threshold"
    "Owner receives alert about emerging issue (e.g., parity trending 0.02% → 0.05%)"
    "Business priority overrides technical risk (e.g., critical user impacting launch)"
    "Application fix is in-flight and owner wants to delay rollback to deploy it"
    "Owner disagrees with automatic trigger threshold and wants investigation time"]}

  :decision-tree/scenario-1-emerging-parity-divergence
  {:scenario "Parity divergence trending upward (0.01% → 0.05% → 0.10%)"
   :automatic-trigger-fires "Only at 1.0% (100x the pre-flight target)"
   :owner-observation "At 0.10%, owner is concerned but automatic trigger has not fired yet"

   :decision-tree
   [{:decision-point "Is parity divergence likely to exceed 1% within next 30 minutes?"
     :assessment
     {:if-yes "YES - parity acceleration evident (0.01% → 0.05% → 0.10% trend)"
      :decision "RECOMMEND MANUAL ROLLBACK (do not wait for automatic trigger)"
      :rationale "Waiting for 1% threshold risks cascading to 5%+ before rollback executes. Parity divergence is data consistency issue (not salvageable by load reduction)."
      :action "Owner: Issue manual rollback command. Escalation-lead logs: '[MANUAL ROLLBACK] Parity trending toward critical. Rolled back at 0.10% to prevent cascade.'"
      :timeline "Rollback executes < 2 min"}
     :if-no "NO - divergence stable or decreasing (e.g., 0.10% → 0.09%)"
      :decision "CONTINUE MONITORING, DO NOT ROLLBACK YET"
      :rationale "If trending downward, may be transient (e.g., specific request type). Monitor for 10 more minutes."
      :action "Monitoring-lead sets escalation: if parity exceeds 0.50%, rollback automatically (lower threshold than 1%)"
      :timeline "Reassess at +10 min"}]

   :owner-override-example
   "Canary-lead: 'Monitoring-lead, parity at 0.08% and trending up. Recommend manual rollback before automatic trigger?'
    Monitoring-lead: 'Agree. Divergence in /api/kgraph/* endpoints. Likely semantic issue, not transient.'
    Canary-lead: 'Initiating manual rollback. Escalation-lead, document this decision.'
    Escalation-lead (Slack): '[MANUAL ROLLBACK] Parity trend analysis: rolled back at 0.08% to prevent cascade. Post-incident review required.'"}

  :decision-tree/scenario-2-application-fix-in-flight
  {:scenario "Latency spike detected (p99 = 105ms), but application team has fix ready (20 min deploy)"
   :automatic-trigger-fires "At p99 = 200ms sustained > 5 min (not yet triggered)"
   :owner-observation "At p99 = 105ms, owner is concerned but within acceptable variance"

   :decision-tree
   [{:decision-point "Can application fix be deployed and verified within 15 minutes?"
     :assessment
     {:if-yes "YES - app team confirms: 'Deploy + restart nodes = 12 min, test = 2 min. Ready?'"
      :decision "GRANT OWNER OVERRIDE: delay rollback, deploy fix"
      :rationale "If fix resolves latency spike, proceeding avoids full canary restart. Higher business value than rollback."
      :sla-constraint "Maximum 15-minute override window. If fix not deployed by then → automatic rollback executes."
      :procedure
      ["Owner issues override in Slack: 'Override rollback for 15 min. Deploying fix. Monitoring continues.'"
       "App team deploys fix: metrics-lead watches for p99 response"
       "At p99 = 98ms post-deploy: 'Fix validated, p99 normal. Override successful.'"
       "If p99 does not improve by +10 min: escalation-lead initiates rollback (5 min remaining)"]
      :action "Escalation-lead logs: '[MANUAL OVERRIDE] Latency spike, app fix deployed. Override: +15 min. Result: p99 recovered to 98ms. Override successful.'"}
     :if-no "NO - app team says: 'Deploy is 30 min minimum (dependency chain)'"
      :decision "DO NOT OVERRIDE, EXECUTE ROLLBACK IMMEDIATELY"
      :rationale "If fix cannot be deployed within 15 min SLA, manual override is not applicable. Automatic recovery (rollback) is better than extended latency."
      :action "Owner: 'Rollback immediately. App fix is separate work stream (retry on next canary).'"
      :timeline "Rollback < 2 min"}]

   :override-sla-strict
   "The 15-minute SLA is **hard limit** (non-negotiable):
    - Owner can delay automatic rollback only if fix is genuinely in-flight
    - Fix must complete, be deployed, and show SLO improvement within 15 min
    - If SLA expires and fix not verified → automatic rollback executes
    - Example: Owner issues override at 14:00 JST. By 14:15 JST, if p99 not improved → rollback fires autonomously"

   :owner-override-example
   "Scenario: Stage 2 ramp to 90%. Latency spike observed (p99 = 110ms).
    Monitoring-lead: 'p99 elevated to 110ms. Auto-trigger threshold is 200ms, not yet firing. But trending up (105ms → 110ms in 3 min).'
    App team (Slack): 'We found bug in session cache lock. Fix ready, deploy in 12 min.'
    Owner: '[OVERRIDE] Delaying rollback 15 min. App team: deploy fix. Monitoring: watch p99 post-deploy. If not recovered by 14:15 → automatic rollback executes.'
    (12 min later) App team: 'Fix deployed. Restarting nodes.'
    (2 min later) Monitoring-lead: 'p99 recovered to 96ms. Fix successful. Override rescinded. Proceeding with Stage 2 ramp.'"

  :decision-tree/scenario-3-false-alert-investigation
  {:scenario "Alert fires: 5xx rate = 1.5% (auto-trigger threshold)"
   :automatic-trigger-fires "YES - 5xx > 1% sustained > 2 min, automatic rollback triggered"
   :owner-observation "But owner suspects false positive (all errors are from single endpoint, likely a test)"

   :critical-note "Automatic rollback has ALREADY EXECUTED. Owner cannot 'delay' it."
   :owner-action "Manual rollback is NOT applicable here. Automatic rollback already happened."
   :post-rollback-investigation
   ["Monitoring-lead retrieves error logs: confirm false positive (e.g., test endpoint spike)"
    "Update alert rules: exclude test endpoints from 5xx count"
    "Document: 'False positive alert, cause: test endpoint spam. Updated alert rules to filter.'"]
   :learning "This is why fire-drill includes false positive scenarios. Alerts may need tuning based on canary experience."

   :key-insight "Manual override does NOT apply to automatic triggers that have already fired.
                 Manual decision is for **preventing** automatic trigger fire, not **undoing** it."

  :decision-tree/scenario-4-business-priority-override
  {:scenario "Latency p99 = 98ms (below trigger), but business priority: 'Must reach 100% traffic for marketing launch'"
   :automatic-trigger-fires "No automatic trigger firing (all SLOs green)"
   :owner-observation "Owner and business team want to skip Stage 3a (90% → 99%) and jump directly to 100%"

   :decision-tree
   [{:decision-point "Do all SLO gates pass for Stage 2 (90% traffic)?"
     :assessment
     {:if-yes "YES - all SLOs green at 90%"
      :decision "Owner can APPROVE Stage 3 (99% → 100%) even if business wants to rush"
      :rationale "SLOs passing means system is healthy. Business priority can be accommodated **within technical constraints**."
      :procedure
      ["Monitoring-lead confirms: 'Stage 2 SLOs: PASS. p99=95ms, parity=0.005%, 5xx=0.001%'"
       "Owner: 'Approved Stage 3 cutover. Escalation-lead, move to 99% ramp immediately.'"
       "Escalation-lead logs: '[STAGE ACCELERATION] Business priority: accelerated to Stage 3 (already met SLO criteria).'"
       "Note: This is NOT an override (no SLA risk). Just faster gate approval."]
      :note "This is not 'manual override' in the sense of violating SLOs. It's just decision velocity."}
     :if-no "NO - SLOs marginal or failing (p99=110ms, memory=450MB)"
      :decision "Owner MUST NOT override for business priority"
      :rationale "Cannot violate technical constraints for business priority. Risk of production incident outweighs marketing timeline."
      :action "Owner communicates to business: 'We must complete Stage 2 validation. Cannot accelerate without SLO risk.'"
      :timeline "Proceed with normal timeline (4h per stage)"}]

   :principle "Business priority influences **when** to proceed (decision velocity), never **whether** to override technical constraints."

  :decision-tree/scenario-5-team-readiness-gap
  {:scenario "Stage 2 SLOs are green, but on-call engineer was unavailable overnight. Team confidence is low."
   :automatic-trigger-fires "No automatic trigger"
   :owner-observation "Owner receives feedback from on-call: 'Overnight was difficult to monitor alerts. Recommend delaying Stage 3.'"

   :decision-tree
   [{:decision-point "Is technical issue (SLO violation) or process issue (team readiness)?"
     :assessment
     {:if-technical-issue "Latency spike, parity divergence, etc."
      :decision "Follow automatic or manual rollback procedures (see Scenarios 1-4)"
      :note "This is not a team readiness issue."}
     :if-process-issue "Team says: 'We need more sleep/rest before final cutover'"
      :decision "Owner can DEFER Stage 3 (hold at 90%) without technical trigger"
      :rationale "Team readiness is important for rapid incident response. If team is not confident, better to delay than risk decision errors under fatigue."
      :procedure
      ["Owner: 'Monitoring-lead, confirm SLOs green for 1 more hour before Stage 3 decision.'"
       "Hold at 90% for extra stabilization (e.g., 6 hours instead of 4)"
       "Allow on-call engineer to rest and return confident"
       "Escalation-lead logs: '[STAGE HOLD] Team readiness: deferred Stage 3 cutover 2 hours. No technical SLO issue. Proceeding when team ready.'"]}]

   :principle "Manual decisions can defer **based on team confidence**, not just technical SLOs. Fatigue-driven errors are production risk."

  :decision-tree/scenario-6-unresolvable-issue
  {:scenario "Memory leak detected in cljc code. Automatic rollback triggered (heap > 512MB). App team says: 'Root cause unknown. Cannot fix in < 1 hour.'"
   :automatic-trigger-fires "YES - memory exhaustion, automatic rollback to previous stage"
   :owner-response "After rollback, owner must decide: retry same stage, or return to Phase 2 investigation?"

   :decision-tree
   [{:decision-point "Can root cause be fixed and deployed within 4 hours?"
     :assessment
     {:if-yes "YES - app team identifies leak, deploys fix, ready for retry at 90%"
      :decision "RETRY same stage with fixed code (no SLA violation, technical resolution)"
      :procedure
      ["After fix deployed: owner approves retry"
       "Escalation-lead logs: '[RETRY STAGE] Memory leak identified and fixed. Retrying Stage 2 (90% ramp) with new build.'"]
      :timeline "Restart Stage 2, full 4h monitoring window"}
     :if-no "NO - root cause unknown, fix will take > 4 hours"
      :decision "RETURN TO PHASE 2 INVESTIGATION (50% / 50% split)"
      :rationale "Cannot safely retry until root cause is understood. Better to pause and debug than to repeatedly trigger rollback."
      :procedure
      ["Owner: 'Return to Phase 2. Allocate 1-week investigation window. Target: retry canary on 2026-09-18.'"
       "App team performs heap dump analysis, identifies leak"
       "Escalation-lead logs: '[RETURN TO PHASE 2] Memory leak unresolved. Investigation: 1 week. Retry canary: 2026-09-18.'"]
      :timeline "1 week investigation + re-validation"}]

   :principle "If unresolvable issue → better to pause than to loop. Incident + retry cycles waste time and risk production stability."

  :decision-tree/escalation-path
  {:stage-1-concern
   {:trigger "Owner or monitoring-lead sees concern (not automatic trigger)"
    :action "Owner: evaluate decision tree scenario (1-6)"
    :decision "Defer / Hold / Rollback / Override"
    :communication "Slack #prod-gates-wave5"}

  :stage-2-blocking-issue
   {:trigger "Multiple consecutive rollbacks (e.g., 3 automatic rollbacks in same stage)"
    :action "Owner escalates to platform-lead + escalation team"
    :decision "Abort canary? Extend Phase 2 investigation? Return to Phase 1?"
    :timeline "Emergency decision call within 1 hour"}

  :stage-3-cutover-abort
   {:trigger "At Stage 3b (99% → 100% cutover) or during graceful drain, critical issue found"
    :action "Owner executes emergency rollback (revert to 99% or earlier)"
    :decision "Keep 1% Rust standby active for next 7 days"
    :communication "Email + Slack to all stakeholders"
    :post-incident "Post-mortem meeting within 24 hours"}}

  :decision-tree/sla-summary
  {:automatic-rollback-sla "< 2 min from trigger condition to traffic revert"
   :manual-override-sla "< 15 min maximum (if owner initiates override). Auto-rollback executes if override expires without resolution."
   :deferral-sla "Up to 2-4 hours (owner can hold stage for additional validation without triggering rollback)"
   :return-to-phase-2-sla "If unresolvable issue: escalate within 1 hour, make return-to-phase-2 decision"}

  :decision-tree/owner-responsibilities
  ["Approve all stage transitions (gates 1-4)"
   "Monitor during stages (via Slack #prod-gates-wave5 dashboard links)"
   "Respond to escalation alerts within 5 minutes (PagerDuty or Slack)"
   "Make override decisions (if fix in-flight, approve up to 15 min delay)"
   "Make deferral decisions (if team needs rest or more validation time)"
   "Escalate blocking issues (multiple rollbacks, unresolvable leak)"
   "Declare cutover complete (2026-09-14 22:00 JST) or abort"]

  :decision-tree/common-mistakes-to-avoid
  [{:mistake "Override automatic rollback without 15-min SLA"
    :consequence "Fix not deployed, SLA expires, rollback fires anyway, canary wastes time"
    :correction "Only grant override if fix deployment + verification is < 15 min"}
   {:mistake "Deferring stage for business priority (marketing launch)"
    :consequence "Team pushed to accelerate despite SLO concerns, increases incident risk"
    :correction "Business priority can influence decision velocity, never override technical constraints"}
   {:mistake "Extending Phase 2 validation indefinitely (decision paralysis)"
    :consequence "Canary never reaches 100%, project timeline slips indefinitely"
    :correction "Set decision deadline (e.g., 'Return to Phase 2 for 1 week max, then retry or abort')"
    :note "Avoid open-ended 'investigate until perfect' mindset"}
   {:mistake "Ignoring team fatigue / readiness gaps"
    :consequence "Tired team makes decision errors, incident response is slow"
    :correction "Use scenario 5: defer stage for team confidence if no SLO issue"}
   {:mistake "Overriding automatic trigger without escalation"
    :consequence "Single person making risky decision without peer review"
    :correction "Always escalate to canary-lead or platform-lead for override approval"}]

  :decision-tree/quick-reference-card
  "**AUTOMATIC TRIGGERS** (fire autonomously, no decision needed):
   - Latency: p99 > 200ms sustained 5+ min → rollback to previous stage
   - Parity: divergence > 1% sustained 1+ min → FULL rollback to Phase 2
   - Reliability: 5xx > 1% sustained 2+ min → rollback to previous stage
   - Memory: heap > 512MB sustained 2+ min → rollback to previous stage

   **MANUAL OVERRIDE** (owner decision, max 15 min SLA):
   - If SLO violation NOT yet at automatic threshold, owner can recommend rollback early
   - If fix in-flight, owner can grant up to 15 min delay for deployment
   - If team needs rest, owner can defer stage (no rollback, hold current traffic)

   **ABORT CANARY** (escalate to platform-lead):
   - Unresolvable issue (memory leak, root cause unknown, fix > 4 hours)
   - Multiple consecutive rollbacks (> 2 in same stage)
   - Business timeline conflict with technical constraints

   **DECISION DEADLINE**: All stage decisions by owner must happen within 2 hours of gate time.
   If no decision by deadline → hold current stage until next review window (4 hours later)."

